  "answer": "This has been reported before. Apps that require UAC elevation, such as HWiNFO, show the UAC prompt when launched from Command Palette, but the app never opens. The same shortcut works from the Start Menu. In #43408 a maintainer found the cause: some apps can't be elevated from the unelevated WinUI3 process Command Palette runs in. The launch fails with a Win32Exception ('No application is associated with the specified file') after the first UAC dialog. The maintainer was looking at ways to launch through a trusted middleman, such as sudo or PowerShell, but I don't see a fix in those tickets. A workaround from #40607 is to open the app's Start Menu shortcut, go to Properties > Compatibility, and enable 'Run this program as administrator'. In #43408 one user had two HWiNFO entries and only one failed, so try the other entry too. PowerToys Run launches these apps without trouble. You can follow or add your details (LenovoLegionToolkit, version 0.100.2) on those tickets."
 },
